WHO supports countries and stakeholders to implement the recommended actions by:

- developing global policies, guidelines and technical guidance based on the best available evidence;
- supporting countries to strengthen national policies, programmes and multisectoral action to promote physical activity;
- providing practical tools, training and capacity-building resources to support implementation across settings and populations;
- convening and coordinating partners across sectors, including health, sport, transport, education and urban planning, to create environments that support active lives; and
- strengthening surveillance, monitoring progress towards global targets, and advancing the evidence base, including through innovations such as wearable technologies and international research collaborations.

WHO supports countries and stakeholders to implement the recommended actions by developing global policy guidance and guidelines, underpinned by latest evidence and consensus, to help countries develop appropriate policies, investment cases and financing mechanisms.

